First Author: Zhou
Title: Predicting heart transplant outcomes using explainable artificial intelligence: a multicenter study
Source number: 76

Very short summary: This retrospective multinational registry study developed the Generalizable Interpretable Neural Network (GINN) using 45,927 UNOS heart transplant recipients and evaluated it in later UNOS cohorts and three geographically external cohorts. In the 15,200-recipient out-of-time UNOS validation cohort, GINN achieved an AUROC of 0.827 (95% CI 0.821–0.833), accuracy of 80%, reported precision of 82%, recall of 80%, and F1-score of 0.81, with good reported calibration; however, important inconsistencies exist between the text, figures, tables, and confusion matrices.

