	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: GINN used an additive Risk Response Network in which each of nine structured clinical variables was processed by a separate lightweight MLP and combined into a mortality-risk logit. The nine inputs were specified a priori from clinical relevance and established heart-transplant risk models; an embedded Lasso-style regularizer promoted sparsity but was not used as preliminary feature screening. Comparators included IMPACT, IHTSA, recalibrated IHTSA, and EBM. Interpretability was intrinsic through feature-specific partial-response curves and additive patient-level risk contributions. Temporal UNOS evaluation and geographic validation in Eurotransplant, Scandiatransplant, and External-CN were performed, but no explicit hyperparameter-search or tuning procedure was reported.

Section 4: AI Quality & Reproducibility (CONVINCE Standards)
