	•	Training Size (N): 45927
	•	Test Size (N): 15200
	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Continuous variables were median-imputed, categorical variables were mode-imputed, and numerical variables were standardized using z-score normalization. Variable coding was harmonized across centers, and SMOTE was applied to the minority mortality class in the training set. The derivation cohort contained 45,927 recipients, an intermediate temporal test cohort contained 20,200, and the primary out-of-time validation cohort contained 15,200. The pipeline was implemented in Python/PyTorch using a fixed random seed. Data access procedures were described, but source code and trained model weights were not reported.

