	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: Performance was extracted for GINN in the 15,200-recipient out-of-time UNOS validation cohort: AUROC 0.827 (95% CI 0.821–0.833), accuracy 0.80, reported precision 0.82, recall 0.80, and F1-score 0.81. Specificity and NPV were not explicitly reported. Calibration was assessed using calibration plots, slope, calibration-in-the-large, Brier score, and expected-to-observed ratio; Table 4 reports slope 1.02, CITL 0.02, Brier score 0.115, and E/O 1.01. DCA was not reported. The reported precision of 0.82 is not reconcilable with the death-class PPV implied by the displayed confusion matrix, and external-cohort AUROCs differ between the narrative/Figure 6 and Table 4.

